    <pageContent>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a58b29f0-29c6-47b8-b8ce-329b38fbed3c",
      "key": "925ba963-d39c-4206-b9ff-626164a11f14",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch2\u003EUmbraco is a highly versatile and cost-effective, open-source content management system.\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EUmbraco can be used to build great websites and other digital experiences. Its open architecture and rich ecosystem of packages make it one of the most flexible platforms available \u2014 whether you\u0027re running a small marketing site or a complex, multi-site enterprise digital experience.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIt\u0027s popular with marketing teams and IT functions alike because of its intuitive editing interface, strong developer tooling, and support for headless delivery alongside traditional rendering.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EUmbraco Platinum Partners\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003E3chillies is proud to be an Umbraco Platinum Partner \u2014 the highest tier of accreditation in the Umbraco partner programme. We\u0027ve been working with the platform for more than a decade, delivering a wide range of Umbraco websites from straightforward marketing sites to large-scale, multi-lingual and multi-site solutions.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWe have been certified Umbraco partners since 2015 and currently have ten Umbraco-certified developers on our team. Our engineers regularly attend Umbraco community events including Codegarden, contribute to the open-source ecosystem, and hold multiple individual Umbraco certifications.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhat can Umbraco do?\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EUmbraco is built on ASP.NET Core and gives developers complete freedom in how they architect and build solutions. Key capabilities include:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EContent Delivery API:\u003C/strong\u003E Umbraco\u0027s built-in headless API lets you deliver content to any front-end technology \u2014 React, Next.js, SvelteKit, native mobile apps and more.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EMulti-site and multi-lingual:\u003C/strong\u003E Manage multiple sites and languages from a single Umbraco installation, with fine-grained permission controls per site or section.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EFlexible content modelling:\u003C/strong\u003E Build exactly the content structures you need using document types, block lists, block grids, and media types \u2014 with no constraints imposed by the platform.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ERich media management:\u003C/strong\u003E A built-in media library with image cropping, focal point control and SVG support keeps assets well-organised and performant.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPackage ecosystem:\u003C/strong\u003E Hundreds of community and commercial packages extend Umbraco with features like forms, search, SEO, commerce and marketing automation.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ECloud or self-hosted:\u003C/strong\u003E Run Umbraco on your own infrastructure, on Azure or AWS, or use the fully managed Umbraco Cloud platform.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhy we love working with Umbraco\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOne of the reasons we love working with the platform is its sheer flexibility. Umbraco places almost no restrictions on how content is structured or how pages are built, which means we can deliver exactly what our clients need rather than working around platform limitations.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOur clients love Umbraco too \u2014 the content management and editing experience has a deserved reputation as being intuitive and easy to use. Non-technical editors can manage complex content structures confidently, reducing reliance on developer support for day-to-day content updates.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBecause Umbraco is open source it has no licensing fees, coming in at a significantly lower price point than some other enterprise platforms, but offering the same depth of features. This makes it an excellent choice for organisations who want enterprise-grade capability without enterprise-level licensing costs.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EUmbraco and headless architecture\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWith the introduction of the Umbraco Content Delivery API in version 12, Umbraco has become a first-class choice for headless and composable architectures. We\u0027ve been building headless Umbraco solutions for clients who want the flexibility of modern front-end frameworks alongside the reliability of a mature CMS.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis very website is built on a headless Umbraco backend \u2014 content is authored in the Umbraco backoffice and delivered via the Content Delivery API to a modern front-end, demonstrating exactly what a headless Umbraco solution looks like in practice.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
